{
 "brief": "Political analyst Wissam Affifah said Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's rejection of a peace council document strikes not only at the agreement itself but puts the Trump administration itself to a political test, according to Shehab Wire. The rejection, Affifah argued, represents far more than a simple disagreement over terms.\n\nThe move places direct political pressure on U.S. leadership to clarify its position and commitment to the peace process. Affifah's assessment suggests Netanyahu's stance on the peace council proposal marks a critical juncture, forcing the Trump administration to demonstrate whether it will push back against Israeli rejection or accommodate the Israeli government's objections.",
